  "source": {
    "doc": "8000series.pdf",
    "page": "6 and 7",
    "section": "Mark 8000 series ordering schematic"
  },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic, ten models in one grammar. The bonnet column splits into its metal and plastic body lists, held to the Kynar and PVC bodies, whose own ends include the bolt-thru row and whose plug list is the plastic one; the angle and three-way models print a single non-standard plug row, so a plug choice on them refuses everything else, exactly as the sheet has it. The motor valve takes its own actuator and range tables. The starred bonnets carry their positioner recommendations, the double starred multi-ply bellows high temperature bonnet requires one, enforced on the plain models through the SMP position, and the actuator size digit runs through the range, limit switch, handwheel and I/P positions as an inferred coupling in the JR manner. The Cv ladder prints its second column out of numeric order, carried exactly.",
